From 04a226dc6a88ce82b155084f99fad25c49d190ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard DEMONGEOT <richard@rdem-systems.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:14:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/51] gui: never split a machine backup into one snapshot per
 disk

All selected disks of a machine backup belong to ONE snapshot: for the
"vm" type its backup-id is the numeric VM ID, which a per-disk split
would turn into non-numeric ids. (The reader/uploader handoff and the
early VM ID check of the former patch are fixed upstream.)
---
 gui/backup_inline.go | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gui/backup_inline.go b/gui/backup_inline.go
index 8887e9b..dc4a66d 100644
--- a/gui/backup_inline.go
+++ b/gui/backup_inline.go
@@ -575,7 +575,9 @@ func RunBackupInline(opts BackupOptions) (returnErr error) {
 	// first), landing as separate snapshots in a single group — which makes prune
 	// keep/drop the wrong folders. A single selected directory keeps the caller's
 	// backup-id (which may have been set explicitly, e.g. by a scheduled job).
-	if len(opts.BackupObjects) <= 1 {
+	// Machine backups are never split: all selected disks belong to ONE "vm"
+	// snapshot whose backup-id is the numeric VM ID (see machinebackuplib).
+	if len(opts.BackupObjects) <= 1 || opts.Kind == "machine" {
 		return runBackupInlineInternal(opts)
 	}
 
